(and to enhance the quality and
realism of the visuals.)

10
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,920
(Warning: This series contains attempted
suicide, blood, and violence.)

11
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:33,920
And this one is for my dad.

12
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:14,760
Ken.

13
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:21,560
I was so close.

14
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:25,360
I nearly caught that villain.

15
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:28,160
Why did you do that?

16
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:33,560
That's no ordinary Nour.

17
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:37,360
Your carelessness could get you killed.

18
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:42,280
I was trying to protect you.

19
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,160
Protect me?

20
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,640
Aren't you just afraid that if he dies,

21
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:58,840
you'll lose your chance
to go back to your true love?

22
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,200
Silence means yes, right?

23
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,760
You still want to die.

24
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,520
Everything I did

25
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:22,120
means nothing to you, does it?

26
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:26,360
I've

27
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,160
tried everything

28
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,440
just so I could live by your side.

29
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:43,880
But you're doing everything

30
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:47,640
just to die and leave me like this?

31
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,880
You're so selfish.

32
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,760
Do you remember what I told you?

33
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:03,400
As long as I'm still alive,

34
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,880
you won't get your wish to die.

35
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:10,680
So I thought it might be better

36
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:16,360
if I just died and ended it all.

37
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,880
How much do you really
understand about death?

38
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:29,480
How many people you loved
have died in front of you?

39
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:35,400
You said I don't understand death.

40
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,600
Don't underestimate me.

41
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,680
Do I have to watch the people I love,

42
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:47,160
the people around me, die one by one?

43
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:50,160
Right now,

44
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:54,120
only one person I love left.

45
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:57,480
It's you.

46
00:03:58,760 --> 00:03:59,360
It's you.

47
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,000
And you

48
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:10,320
still want to get back
at me by killing yourself?

49
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:14,360
In the end,

50
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:18,360
everyone leaves me.

51
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,320
I should never have loved you.

52
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:08,120
(A WeTV Original Series)

53
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:41,720
=Nour=
(WeTV Original)

54
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:44,280
Can anyone explain all of this to me?

55
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,520
All these mistakes

56
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:51,200
are on Inspector Ken, sir.

57
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,880
We lost Officer Pimfan

58
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:58,080
because Inspector Kiran's plan
wasn't detailed enough.

59
00:05:58,240 --> 00:05:59,840
- She too gave her life
- Who's there?

60
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:01,640
- complete the mission.
- Someone help us!

61
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:03,560
We're still investigating

62
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,920
whether Dr. Jiratikarn

63
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,760
was involved in Officer Pimfan's death

64
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:09,000
and whether he was
working with Chidtawan.

65
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,400
I've assigned officers to keep
Dr. Jiratikarn under surveillance

66
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:12,840
in case anything suspicious comes up.

67
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,320
As for Inspector Kiran,

68
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:18,080
I'd like you to consider suspending him
and investigating the matter, sir.

69
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,720
I request permission to lead the team
personally in arresting Chidtawan, sir.

70
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:27,040
All right, Inspector James.
You may lead the team.

71
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:30,000
We must get Chidtawan,

72
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,640
dead or alive.

73
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,440
Understood?

74
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,520
- Understood, sir.
- Understood, sir.

75
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,480
Phong, shut down the computer.
Meeting adjourned.

76
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:50,240
Are you sure you want to do that?

77
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:55,600
That's the plan.

78
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:45,280
Ji.

79
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:48,320
Get up and have a bite, sweetheart.

80
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:50,240
Hmm?

81
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:56,680
I want to be alone, Mom.

82
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:21,440
I'm never going to recover, am I?

83
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:29,640
You already know the answer.

84
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:31,440
Dr. Jirat.

85
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:40,640
Yes.

86
00:10:43,920 --> 00:10:44,360
But

87
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:46,640
I really can't accept it.

88
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:52,400
You know I've hurt my family before.

89
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:55,360
And look at me now.

90
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:59,280
I've tried cutting my arm so many times,
but nothing happens.

91
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,840
There's not even a scratch.

92
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:07,760
So what are you going to do next?

93
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:21,360
I'd probably run far away.

94
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:27,480
No matter how much I love my family,

95
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:33,760
I understand now that I need to stay
as far away from them as possible.

96
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:38,840
What about Chita?

97
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:44,040
He's the only one
who can stay with you right now.

98
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:03,640
Being with him

99
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,160
makes me happy.

100
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:10,080
I used to be happy.

101
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:16,280
That was before
I knew who he really was.

102
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:21,760
Even now,
I still can't believe someone like him

103
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:23,320
could have killed so many people.

104
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,400
You're not answering my question.

105
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:53,720
I love him.

106
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:57,280
I love him.

107
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:04,280
I don't know either.

108
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:06,960
Maybe I'll choose to stay with him.

109
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,080
Because soon,

110
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,680
I'll become a monster just like him.

111
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:25,360
What about you?

112
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:34,960
What are you going to do next?

113
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:38,400
I heard you were suspended.

114
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,200
I've lived far too long already.

115
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:13,600
I hope you made the right choice.

116
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:22,640
Can I ask you something?

117
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:28,320
Have you ever thought
that maybe staying alive

118
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:31,400
could be the right answer?

119
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:45,400
Of course.

120
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:14,360
I can still picture myself
dancing with him every New Year's Eve.

121
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:25,640
I can picture James having more records
than I've collected in 200 years.

122
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:28,120
The soundtrack from this movie.
I really love watching it.

123
00:15:29,960 --> 00:15:34,400
I can picture James and me
being happy together every day.

124
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,360
Okay, okay.

125
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:36,720
Don't open your eyes yet.

126
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:41,000
Ready?

127
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:41,880
Mm.

128
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:42,800
You can open your eyes now.

129
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:45,480
What's this?

130
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:47,920
It's behind you.

131
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:50,880
When you're ready, turn around.

132
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:54,320
Three, two, one.

133
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:56,040
Turn around.

134
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:07,240
This time,

135
00:16:07,880 --> 00:16:10,520
I brought you to see it up close,
just like I promised.

136
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:19,240
What? You're not happy?

137
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:21,720
I am.

138
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:26,680
Come on, let me take a picture for you.

139
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:35,560
Let me take it.

140
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:38,920
I learned from you.

141
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:56,760
But I can also see our happiness
coming to an end.

142
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,120
Here.

143
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:12,120
I made your favorite food.

144
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:13,760
The best in the world.

145
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:18,800
Are you sure you can travel like this?

146
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:20,920
That's so sudden.

147
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:26,920
Is that why you've been acting strange?

148
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:29,800
Were you worried about me
and afraid to tell me?

149
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:33,720
Yes.

150
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:39,480
Here, your favorite basil stir-fry.

151
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:43,280
Eat plenty, sweetheart.

152
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:44,480
Thanks, Mom.

153
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:49,240
Let's eat.

154
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:54,440
When you're over there,
will you miss my cooking?

155
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:55,800
Hmm?

156
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,360
Of course I will.

157
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:08,120
Oh.

158
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:10,560
What's wrong, sweetheart?

159
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:14,120
Why aren't you eating?

160
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:19,920
The basil stir-fry is spicy, Mom.

161
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:23,920
Burn a hole in your stomach

162
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:28,480
He likes spicy food,
so I have to make it his way.

163
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:33,760
He's going to be there for a long time.
He won't be back for a year, kid.

164
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:37,920
It's really spicy, Mom.

165
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:39,720
Spicy, spicy.

166
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:43,880
Come try this. Want something mild?

167
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:44,400
- Here.
- Sure.

168
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:46,440
- This'll help with the spice.
- Why is the basil so spicy, Mom?

169
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:49,200
Don't you like spicy food?

170
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:52,160
Here, this will help with the spiciness.

171
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:25,000
OK, nice.

172
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:50,480
Your hands are covered in cuts.

173
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:54,240
Don't worry about me.

174
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,760
The more you worry about me,

175
00:19:57,720 --> 00:19:59,200
the harder it is for me.

176
00:20:00,840 --> 00:20:01,520
Of course I'm worried.

177
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,160
You're not Nour.

178
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:07,080
Your wounds won't heal that easily.

179
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:09,600
What if I were Nour?

180
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:16,160
If I could live a long life with you,

181
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:19,240
would you change your mind

182
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:21,920
and want to keep on living?

183
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:25,640
Don't become like me.

184
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:30,080
I want you to move forward

185
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:32,720
and live a happy life.

186
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:38,760
Live a happy life

187
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:40,680
without you?

188
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:51,280
I understand now.

189
00:20:55,560 --> 00:20:56,360
That mirror,

190
00:20:58,240 --> 00:20:59,680
no matter how hard I try to fix it,

191
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,720
it can never go back to the way it was.

192
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:08,880
But no matter what,

193
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:12,000
I still want to keep it.

194
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:18,040
Same with our relationship.

195
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:23,400
No matter how broken it is,

196
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:27,920
I still want to do everything I can

197
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:30,520
to put it back together.

198
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:42,120
But if you still won't change
your mind and still want to die,

199
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:44,880
I'm ready to understand your choice.

200
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:49,240
Please understand me too.

201
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:54,600
I can't just let you die

202
00:21:56,520 --> 00:21:58,440
without doing anything.

203
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:41,760
Yeah.

204
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:50,280
Let's make every moment count
until the very end.

205
00:22:53,560 --> 00:22:54,040
Mm.

206
00:22:55,520 --> 00:22:56,280
I promise

207
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,760
I'll never let you go.

208
00:23:12,160 --> 00:23:13,320
Stop crying.

209
00:23:13,920 --> 00:23:14,520
Come here.

210
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:18,360
Come see how well I fixed the mirror.

211
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:23,040
What do you think? Isn't it beautiful?

212
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:26,640
I think your mirror looks nice.

213
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:30,280
You really have great taste
in everything.

214
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:40,200
How's the packing going?

215
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:42,200
Come sit here.

216
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:50,560
Please take care of Mom for me.

217
00:23:52,520 --> 00:23:54,200
I've written down everything
you need to do

218
00:23:55,440 --> 00:23:56,400
in this notebook.

219
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:02,440
Whoa.

220
00:24:04,760 --> 00:24:05,800
That's a lot.

221
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:08,880
Aren't you only going for a year?

222
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:12,760
Come back and take care of it yourself.

223
00:24:16,640 --> 00:24:17,080
Nin.

224
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:23,600
I'm sorry.

225
00:24:25,560 --> 00:24:26,400
Sorry about what?

226
00:24:28,280 --> 00:24:29,440
You got a scholarship.

227
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:32,040
Just

228
00:24:33,520 --> 00:24:34,680
be happy, okay?

229
00:24:37,120 --> 00:24:39,720
From now on, whatever path you choose,

230
00:24:41,880 --> 00:24:44,760
I hope it leads you to a bright future.

231
00:24:56,880 --> 00:24:57,880
I'm sorry.

232
00:25:10,360 --> 00:25:11,720
I should've spent more time with you.

233
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:16,640
I should've made more time for you.

234
00:25:18,320 --> 00:25:19,680
It's okay.

235
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:23,560
But I've made my decision, Nin.

236
00:25:25,080 --> 00:25:26,040
For Mom and for you.

237
00:25:27,800 --> 00:25:29,120
I'm proud of you.

238
00:25:33,320 --> 00:25:35,080
From now on,
you have to stay strong for Mom.

239
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:38,520
Come here. Give me a hug.

240
00:25:39,440 --> 00:25:41,120
- Give me a hug.
- Hey, no hugging for grown-ups.

241
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,120
I'm leaving.

242
00:25:44,920 --> 00:25:45,440
Okay.

243
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:48,400
I'm glad you're my brother.

244
00:25:50,880 --> 00:25:51,760
I'm glad too

245
00:25:52,440 --> 00:25:53,400
that you're my brother.

246
00:25:55,040 --> 00:25:55,840
I'm leaving.

247
00:26:31,280 --> 00:26:32,360
Don't cry, sweetheart.

248
00:26:33,520 --> 00:26:35,120
I was trying so hard not to cry.

249
00:26:36,960 --> 00:26:38,600
It's only a year, sweetheart.

250
00:26:57,920 --> 00:26:59,160
Your brother's got a stomachache.

251
00:26:59,360 --> 00:27:02,720
If he still hasn't gotten better,
Rain'll take him to the doctor tonight.

252
00:27:04,320 --> 00:27:05,680
Don't worry, sweetheart.

253
00:27:39,400 --> 00:27:40,840
Take care of Mom for me, Nin.

254
00:27:41,760 --> 00:27:42,040
I will.

255
00:27:46,560 --> 00:27:49,800
I'll take good care of myself.
Don't worry, sweetheart.

256
00:28:02,880 --> 00:28:04,080
Travel safe.

257
00:28:04,200 --> 00:28:05,280
Travel safe, sweetheart.

258
00:28:34,440 --> 00:28:35,120
Are you ready?

259
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:46,480
I'm ready.

260
00:28:51,320 --> 00:28:52,320
At least

261
00:28:54,080 --> 00:28:55,480
my family is safe.

262
00:28:58,480 --> 00:28:59,280
I just wish

263
00:29:00,960 --> 00:29:02,640
I could be there
to see my brother happy,

264
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:06,640
to be there on his graduation day,

265
00:29:08,440 --> 00:29:10,120
and to see Mom smile.

266
00:29:17,880 --> 00:29:19,160
I really wish I could.

267
00:29:29,640 --> 00:29:31,040
You seem human today.

268
00:30:06,360 --> 00:30:07,360
I brought him here.

269
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:22,160
Don't forget what we agreed on.

270
00:30:25,360 --> 00:30:26,520
Why did you help me that day?

271
00:30:30,720 --> 00:30:31,760
We are the same.

272
00:30:36,800 --> 00:30:37,960
I promise you

273
00:30:40,080 --> 00:30:41,680
I'll let you see Dr. Ji again

274
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:46,960
if you give me what I want.

275
00:30:52,840 --> 00:30:53,880
What do you want?

276
00:30:56,560 --> 00:30:57,480
Nour like us

277
00:30:58,520 --> 00:30:59,600
don't want much.

278
00:31:06,320 --> 00:31:07,440
Kill me.

279
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:49,080
What you're doing

280
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:53,680
is good for you, isn't it?

281
00:32:10,160 --> 00:32:11,080
Hey, watch out.

282
00:32:18,680 --> 00:32:20,000
Do you think that just by dying,

283
00:32:20,680 --> 00:32:23,000
you can repay the life
you owe your true love?

284
00:32:25,560 --> 00:32:26,440
No matter what,

285
00:32:28,080 --> 00:32:29,640
please don't turn me into a Nour.

286
00:32:39,360 --> 00:32:40,800
I'll find the culprit

287
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:43,920
and the person who killed
my father as soon as possible.

288
00:32:46,640 --> 00:32:48,480
Because I want to
start living my life with you

289
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:51,240
as soon as I can.

290
00:33:09,880 --> 00:33:10,760
Ken.

291
00:33:12,040 --> 00:33:13,240
That's enough.

292
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:16,160
I'm begging you.

293
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,040
Stop there.

294
00:33:22,480 --> 00:33:23,040
Go back.

295
00:33:24,040 --> 00:33:25,000
I'm not going back.

296
00:33:26,040 --> 00:33:28,280
I know you don't really want to die.

297
00:33:29,360 --> 00:33:30,320
I know.

298
00:33:31,320 --> 00:33:32,280
I can see

299
00:33:33,600 --> 00:33:35,000
that you're scared.

300
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:37,440
You're scared

301
00:33:38,280 --> 00:33:39,160
of dying.

302
00:33:40,720 --> 00:33:41,800
You're scared

303
00:33:42,640 --> 00:33:43,800
of leaving me.

304
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:45,760
You're scared

305
00:33:46,840 --> 00:33:48,680
that you won't get to live
your life with me anymore.

306
00:33:50,240 --> 00:33:51,600
I can see it.

307
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:53,480
Do you think I'm stupid?

308
00:34:01,720 --> 00:34:02,840
All this time,

309
00:34:04,080 --> 00:34:05,920
we've been so happy together,
haven't we?

310
00:34:08,640 --> 00:34:10,040
You were happy with me.

311
00:34:12,240 --> 00:34:13,080
You smiled

312
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:15,800
for the first time in hundreds of years

313
00:34:16,680 --> 00:34:17,560
because of me.

314
00:34:20,920 --> 00:34:22,160
And I was happy

315
00:34:27,320 --> 00:34:28,240
I know

316
00:34:29,240 --> 00:34:31,680
you've wanted to die
for hundreds of years.

317
00:34:32,760 --> 00:34:34,880
But I made you
change your mind, didn't I?

318
00:34:38,640 --> 00:34:39,880
I showed you

319
00:34:42,120 --> 00:34:44,400
that living like an ordinary human

320
00:34:46,160 --> 00:34:47,720
can bring so much happiness.

321
00:34:52,120 --> 00:34:53,800
Every time we danced together,

322
00:34:57,720 --> 00:34:59,320
you smiled so happily.

323
00:35:00,600 --> 00:35:02,560
You smiled
from the bottom of your heart.

324
00:35:03,720 --> 00:35:04,840
And I saw it.

325
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:08,400
Every time I ate the noodles you made,

326
00:35:11,280 --> 00:35:12,440
you'd secretly watch me

327
00:35:13,360 --> 00:35:14,480
to see if I liked them.

328
00:35:15,400 --> 00:35:16,960
And I really loved them.

329
00:35:20,960 --> 00:35:22,080
My life

330
00:35:23,280 --> 00:35:24,480
is just this simple.

331
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:25,320
Ken.

332
00:35:31,080 --> 00:35:32,080
Just say it.

333
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:36,040
Say that you want to live with me too.

334
00:35:49,760 --> 00:35:50,520
Move in.

335
00:36:01,200 --> 00:36:02,480
Let me finish this first.

336
00:36:19,360 --> 00:36:19,880
Chita.

337
00:36:21,200 --> 00:36:22,120
Hey, stop shooting!

338
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:38,000
I said stop shooting!

339
00:36:40,680 --> 00:36:41,160
Run!

340
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:44,640
Run!

341
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:02,040
Chita.

342
00:37:06,760 --> 00:37:07,840
In this world,

343
00:37:09,680 --> 00:37:12,120
is there really somewhere
we can live together?

344
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:19,200
You don't hate me anymore, Doctor?

345
00:37:22,080 --> 00:37:22,840
I don't know.

346
00:37:25,040 --> 00:37:26,640
I just don't want you to hurt anyone,

347
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:29,560
and I don't want anyone to hurt you.

348
00:37:38,920 --> 00:37:40,800
No matter how cruel the world is to me,

349
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:49,080
I still have you,

350
00:37:50,840 --> 00:37:51,960
who has always been kind to me.

351
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:01,960
But you've been
lying to me all this time.

352
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:10,480
Look at your legs now.

353
00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:15,760
The Chita I knew as a rescue worker,

354
00:38:20,680 --> 00:38:22,480
the Chita I knew as my assistant,

355
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:29,480
or

356
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:38,360
the Chita I knew as my lover,

357
00:38:45,760 --> 00:38:47,120
I don't know anything about you.

358
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:56,520
Doctor.

359
00:39:00,480 --> 00:39:01,320
I am who I am.

360
00:39:03,600 --> 00:39:04,200
Chita,

361
00:39:05,400 --> 00:39:06,200
your Chita.

362
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:10,640
Come with me first.

363
00:39:15,480 --> 00:39:16,600
Then I'll tell you everything.

364
00:39:21,880 --> 00:39:23,320
How can I trust you, Chita?

365
00:40:02,080 --> 00:40:06,360
(48 years ago, 1978 AD)

366
00:40:19,120 --> 00:40:19,800
What's wrong?

367
00:40:20,480 --> 00:40:21,320
My back is itchy.

368
00:40:23,120 --> 00:40:23,760
Scratch it for me.

369
00:40:27,760 --> 00:40:28,440
Where?

370
00:40:28,880 --> 00:40:29,640
On the right.

371
00:40:29,920 --> 00:40:30,960
Right.

372
00:40:31,560 --> 00:40:32,120
Here?

373
00:40:32,520 --> 00:40:33,760
You can use your hand.

374
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:43,200
- You don't get it at all.
- Sorry.

375
00:40:46,240 --> 00:40:46,960
Here?

376
00:41:05,160 --> 00:41:05,840
Athit.

377
00:41:06,280 --> 00:41:07,000
What?

378
00:41:07,880 --> 00:41:08,880
The clock

379
00:41:10,200 --> 00:41:10,800
stopped.

380
00:41:15,200 --> 00:41:16,080
This one?

381
00:41:25,800 --> 00:41:26,640
Is it good now?

382
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:27,720
There.

383
00:41:55,160 --> 00:41:56,240
Can you promise me

384
00:42:02,480 --> 00:42:03,120
that

385
00:42:06,320 --> 00:42:08,040
you won't turn me into Nour?

386
00:42:13,280 --> 00:42:13,760
Of course.

387
00:42:16,120 --> 00:42:16,800
I promise.

388
00:42:30,120 --> 00:42:30,760
Athit.

389
00:42:31,040 --> 00:42:33,280
Should we buy more plants?

390
00:42:34,120 --> 00:42:34,520
Sure.

391
00:42:35,920 --> 00:42:37,600
How about putting one here?

392
00:42:40,640 --> 00:42:41,160
Mm.

393
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:43,440
But

394
00:42:46,040 --> 00:42:46,800
look.

395
00:42:47,560 --> 00:42:48,680
It's blooming.

396
00:42:51,320 --> 00:42:52,480
We've been watering it for so long.

397
00:42:52,760 --> 00:42:53,360
It's beautiful, isn't it?

398
00:42:54,840 --> 00:42:55,720
It took so long to bloom.

399
00:42:58,160 --> 00:42:59,280
Turn and look at me.

400
00:43:00,360 --> 00:43:02,040
- Let me take a picture of you.
- Hey, no.

401
00:43:02,040 --> 00:43:02,760
Come on.

402
00:43:03,280 --> 00:43:05,400
One, two, three.

403
00:43:09,520 --> 00:43:10,040
Sweet.

404
00:43:12,720 --> 00:43:13,480
Definitely sweet.

405
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:15,440
- Let me see.
- No.

406
00:43:16,880 --> 00:43:17,560
I'm not letting you see it.

407
00:43:17,560 --> 00:43:18,680
- Let me see.
- No.

408
00:43:22,160 --> 00:43:22,760
Is it sweet?

409
00:43:28,040 --> 00:43:29,480
I like it. Do you?

410
00:43:31,080 --> 00:43:31,640
I do.

411
00:43:32,080 --> 00:43:32,680
Like the picture?

412
00:43:35,280 --> 00:43:36,400
Don't even ask.

413
00:43:54,440 --> 00:43:55,360
Why are you back so soon?

414
00:44:16,120 --> 00:44:16,920
Darn!

415
00:44:30,640 --> 00:44:31,240
Chita.

416
00:44:33,320 --> 00:44:34,080
Wait a second.

417
00:44:38,320 --> 00:44:39,440
Darn!

418
00:44:46,560 --> 00:44:47,120
Hey!

419
00:44:48,520 --> 00:44:49,200
Hey!

420
00:44:50,360 --> 00:44:51,560
Stay with me.

421
00:44:53,080 --> 00:44:54,280
Please be okay.

422
00:44:55,720 --> 00:44:56,560
Hey!

423
00:44:58,080 --> 00:44:58,640
Hey!

424
00:44:59,280 --> 00:45:00,760
Stay with me.

425
00:45:15,120 --> 00:45:16,040
I'm sorry.

426
00:46:57,320 --> 00:46:58,920
Ever since the day I was changed,

427
00:47:00,440 --> 00:47:02,040
I instantly knew I was special.

428
00:47:08,320 --> 00:47:09,320
Please don't.

429
00:47:09,400 --> 00:47:11,040
Please, I don't want to die yet.

430
00:47:11,320 --> 00:47:13,040
I don't want to die yet.

431
00:47:13,360 --> 00:47:13,840
Please.

432
00:47:16,200 --> 00:47:17,440
A flame fueled by vengeance for Nour,

433
00:47:22,560 --> 00:47:24,160
Not caring who they are,

434
00:47:24,880 --> 00:47:25,640
Or what they used to be.

435
00:47:26,960 --> 00:47:27,920
Just die.

436
00:47:35,480 --> 00:47:36,640
But then I met you.

437
00:47:42,440 --> 00:47:43,480
Come on, I'll help you.

438
00:47:44,240 --> 00:47:44,720
Hey!

439
00:47:45,960 --> 00:47:46,920
I'm sorry.

440
00:48:11,600 --> 00:48:12,760
It's okay. I'm used to it.

441
00:48:14,640 --> 00:48:15,400
It's going to be okay.

442
00:48:18,440 --> 00:48:19,680
I believe you'll get better.

443
00:48:29,560 --> 00:48:30,760
You understand me, right?

444
00:48:38,200 --> 00:48:39,600
Hey, you guys!

445
00:48:39,600 --> 00:48:40,600

